WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
[Scott] Right. Okay.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.660
And so tell us about what is Waive
and how you came to realise

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.560
there was a problem
that you felt you could fix?

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.450
[James] Yeah. The problem we're trying
to fix is something called the advice gap,

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.900
which affects millions
of people in the UK.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.710
We recognise the gap, it's well
documented. It's basically the gap where

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.800
people need financial advice
but can't afford it.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.660
Only very few people can afford
to have it, but everybody needs it,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.560
especially with things like
auto-enrolment, which is encouraging

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.840
everybody to start saving
into pensions.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.340
But ultimately, everybody needs
personalised advice,

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.040
and today they don't get it.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.410
So Waive is a product
that's built to

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.640
automate financial advice for everybody,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.080
to make sure that financial advice
is inclusive,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.000
accessible and affordable –
most importantly, for everybody.
